    "path": "/longContentPages/0",
    "raw": "There are new worlds across the cosmos awaiting exploration. The next few pages will detail some of them. Note that there are many more than listed.\n\nBiomes can appear around different types of stars, and some appear only in specific stars. For example: You will never find an ^orange;Infernus^reset; around a ^white;Gentle Star^reset;.\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Star Types^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nGentle Star\nTemperate\nRadioactive\nFrozen\nFiery\nBinary\nRed\nBlue\nBlack\nDying\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Bog^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nRich in algae, muck, and plant life. They are ripe with rainy weather, and thick swamps. Travel can be difficult, but the surplus algae will be useful.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Rainforest^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nTeeming with plantlife, Rainforests have rich soil, far exceeding the capacity of ordinary dirt. They host a wide array of wildlife, including plenty of bees.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Crystalline^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nA rich source of silicon (thanks to the extraction of Purple Crystal) and ^yellow;Lunari^reset; crystals. Watch out for the crystal rain, though.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Gelatinous^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nGreat for genetic material. Definitely don't try the lettuce, unless you really like flavorless gelatin soup squishing in your mouth. If you need goopy stuff, this is your first stop.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Proto World^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese bizarre planets are not inhospitable, but the natural biological slime there can melt your flesh. Plus the slime storms, ew. And really, really weird plant life. But they are the only place to get the extremely valuable protocite. You'll need it. Also be advised that the atmosphere contains bizarre bacteria that affect unconditioned lifeforms negatively. Use caution when exploring.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Ice Waste^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nIce wastes are absolutely terrifyingly cold. Don't swim in the water or you'll freeze even faster. They do have some unique sorts of ice there, which provide something extra when extracting. Furthermore, valuable Isogen ore is plentiful on them.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Sulphuric^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese are among the harshest environments you'll encounter. Every moment on a sulphur world is lethal. Deadly winds, blowing debris, no oxygen. Lovely. But, they are extremely rich in Sulphur. Not the place for a summer house, though. Yet people keep trying...\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Penumbra^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nPitch black for most of their existence, these rare worlds have some sort of environmental barrier to the sun. A natural sunglasses-effect in the ozone, or something. Whatever the case...dark and spooky.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Wasteland^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nOnce bustling populations lived on these desolate rocks. Now, their ruins stud the surface like discarded refuse. Technology may remain that can be scavenged, and there is no shortage of Spare Parts if you are looking for some.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Irradiated^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese radioactive rocks are curiously abundant in native life. Granted, it's not edible and you still don't want to hang out there too much. You'll find heaps of radioactive resources here, obviously.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Infernus^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nI'd not suggest going here without a lot of protection. Their surfaces are far from hospitable. They are teeming with danger of every sort, but the allure of Pyreite ore is hard to resist.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Frozen Moon^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese frigid moons are quaint, and not altogether threatening. No life walks on their surfaces. On account of the whole no-air thing.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Nitrogen Sea^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nDoesn't this sound like a fun place to swim? Yea, it really isn't. Some handy liquid there, though.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Cybersphere^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nSomeone, at some point, built these impossibly huge constructs in space. How these were ever engineered remains a hotly contested debate among the scientific community.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Primeval Forest^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nHuge trees, lots of wildlife and abundant natural resources make these a wonderful place to visit. Typically not too dangerous, but watch your back anyhow...you never know what lurks in these huge forests. I've heard rumors of titanic reptiles standing 10 or more metres in the air!\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Atropus^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nA violation of all things decent, Atropus planets are both living and dead. They are quite literally composed of flesh, and some even believe them to be sentient. How they are even possible remains unknown but there is no doubt it is unnatural in every sense of tthe word.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Mountainous^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nWhile it is probably fairly obvious by the name, I have been instructed to inform you that these worlds are rather bumpy and mountainy. They are rich in resources, possessing more metal than most biomes (other than Sulphuric) including rare Zerchesium ore.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Tidewater^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nThese oceans are vastly more rocky and unstable than typical water planets. They generally lack tropical islands, but if you love rocky terrain and coral reefs they might be right up your alley. Through Tidewater, explorers have found unusual nodules capable of scientific miracles.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Lightless^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese unusual worlds are ancient and something prevents any sun from reaching their surfaces. There may be some useful things there, however. Bring lots of lights!\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
    "value": "每个星域都有新的世界等待探索。接下来的几页将详细介绍其中部分内容。请注意，实际内容远不止这些。\n\n有些生物群落可出现在不同类型的恒星周围，而有些仅出现在特定恒星附近。例如：您永远无法在^white;和平的星^reset;周围找到^orange;炼狱^reset;环境。\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;恒星种类^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n和平的星\n温和的星\n放射性星\n寒冷的星\n炽热的星\n双子星\n红星\n蓝星\n黑星\n死星\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;沼泽^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n富含藻类、淤泥和植物。这些星球多雨，沼泽茂密。行进可能较为困难，但丰富的藻类资源非常实用。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;雨林^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n雨林充满植物，土壤肥沃，远超普通泥土。这些星球上有多种野生动物，包括大量蜜蜂。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;结晶^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n富含硅资源（可从紫色晶体中提取）和^yellow;月晶^reset;晶体。但需当心水晶雨。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;凝胶^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n获取遗传物质的理想地点。绝对不要尝试这里的生菜，除非您真的喜欢无味的凝胶汤在嘴里挤压的感觉。如果您需要粘稠物质，这里将是您的首选。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;原毒世界^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这些奇特行星并非不宜居，但天然的生物粘泥会融化您的血肉。加上粘泥风暴，呃。还有非常、非常怪异的植物。但这里是获取极珍贵的原毒矿的唯一来源，您将来会需要它。还需注意，大气中含有怪异细菌，会对未适应的生命形式产生负面影响。探索时请务必小心。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;冰冻荒原^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n冰冻荒原极度寒冷。不要在水中游泳，否则会更快结冰。这里确实有独特的冰种，提取时可提供额外物质。此外，珍贵的异种矿资源也十分丰富。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;硫酸^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这是您将遇到的最恶劣的环境之一。在硫酸星球上的每一刻都致命。致命狂风、飞扬碎片、没有氧气。真不错。不过这些星球富含硫资源。这里绝非避暑胜地。然而总有人不断尝试...\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;半影^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这些稀有世界大部分时间漆黑一片，对太阳存在某种环境屏障。臭氧层或类似物质产生了天然太阳镜效果。无论如何……黑暗而令人毛骨悚然。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;废土^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n曾经繁华的族群居住在这些荒芜的星球上。如今，它们的废墟如废弃垃圾般散布地表。可能有可搜寻的技术残留，若您需要零件，这里不乏备件。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;辐射^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这些放射性岩石上奇特地充满了本土生命。当然，它们不可食用，您也不会想在此久留。显然，这里能找到大量放射性资源。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;炼狱^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n不建议在没有充分防护的情况下前往。这些星球的地表极不适宜停留，充满各种危险，但永燃矿石的诱惑令人难以抗拒。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;冰冻卫星^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这些严寒的卫星古怪却不完全危险。由于完全没有空气，地表并无飞禽走兽。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;液氮海^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这听起来像是个有趣的游泳地点吗？不，完全不是。不过那里有些实用的液体。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;金属卫星^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n在某个时间点，有人在太空中建造了这些不可思议的巨型结构。它们是如何被设计出来的，至今仍是科学界激烈辩论的话题。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;原始森林^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n参天巨木、丰富野生动物和充沛自然资源使这里成为绝佳探访地。通常不算太危险，但无论如何请保持警惕...您永远不知道这些广袤森林中潜伏着什么。我听说有传言称那儿存在高达十米的巨型生物！\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;肉源^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n违背一切常理，肉源星球既生又死。它们完全由血肉构成，甚至有人认为它们具有感知能力。它们如何存在仍属未知，但毫无疑问这在任何意义上都不自然。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;山脉^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n虽然名称已说明一切，但我仍会告知您这些世界崎岖多山。它们资源丰富，金属储量超过大多数生态群系（除硫酸星球外），包括稀有的极熔金矿。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;潮汐^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这里的海洋比起典型水行星的来说有着更多岩石且不稳定。通常没有热带岛屿，但若您喜欢岩石地形和珊瑚礁，它们可能正合您意。探险者通过潮汐世界发现了能实现科学奇迹的特殊结核。\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;无光^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n这些异常世界古老而神秘，某种存在阻止阳光抵达地表。但那里可能有些有用的东西。记得多带光源！\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;Frackin百科\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n如需百科帮助，请使用我们的^cyan;官方wiki^reset;：\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;请勿使用^reset;Fandom的wiki，其中的内容已严重过时。"
  }
]